1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12654,"number":3,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 11:31 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":109211,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":7417,"text":"<p>Compute $\\textrm E\\left[-\\dfrac{1}{3}\\right].$</p>\n","choice1":"$-\\dfrac{1}{3}$","choice2":"$\\dfrac{1}{3}$","choice3":"$-3$","choice4":"$3$","choice5":"$-\\dfrac{1}{9}$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>For any constant $a,$ we have</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\textrm E[a] = a.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Therefore,</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\textrm E\\left[-\\dfrac{1}{3}\\right] = -\\dfrac{1}{3}.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2836,"name":"Properties of Expectation for Discrete Random Variables"},"example":{"id":7417,"title":"Computing the Expected Value of a Constant"},"group":{"id":93942,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14263367,"answer":{"id":62369675,"cread":"2026-10-16T11:31:03.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12654},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62369700,"created":"2026-10-16T11:31:21.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":4,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14322,"number":4,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 11:31 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":109217,"format":"MC","difficulty":3,"exampleId":7417,"text":"<p>Compute $\\textrm E[f^2-2g],$ where $f$ and $g$ are constants.</p>\n","choice1":"$f^2-2g$","choice2":"$f^2$","choice3":"$-2f^2g$","choice4":"$0$","choice5":"$-2g$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>For any constant $a,$ we have</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\textrm E[a] = a.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Therefore,</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\textrm E[f^2-2g] = f^2-2g.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2836,"name":"Properties of Expectation for Discrete Random Variables"},"example":{"id":7417,"title":"Computing the Expected Value of a Constant"},"group":{"id":93944,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14263367,"answer":{"id":62369700,"cread":"2026-10-16T11:31:21.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":4,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14322},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62369731,"created":"2026-10-16T11:31:40.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15706,"number":5,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 11:31 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:16","question":{"id":84093,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7417,"text":"<p>Compute $\\textrm E[c+2],$ where $c$ is a constant.</p>\n","choice1":"$c+2$","choice2":"$c$","choice3":"$2$","choice4":"$2c$","choice5":"$0$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>For any constant $a,$ we have</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\textrm E[a] = a.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Therefore,</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\textrm E[c+2] = c+2.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2836,"name":"Properties of Expectation for Discrete Random Variables"},"example":{"id":7417,"title":"Computing the Expected Value of a Constant"},"group":{"id":93943,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14263367,"answer":{"id":62369731,"cread":"2026-10-16T11:31:40.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15706},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":7418,"number":2,"title":"Computing the Expected Value of a Scaled Random Variable","answers":[{"id":62369768,"created":"2026-10-16T11:32:04.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12438,"number":6,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 11:32 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":84098,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":7418,"text":"<p>Compute $\\textrm E\\left[\\dfrac{1}{2}X\\right]$ if $\\textrm E[X]=6.$</p>\n","choice1":"$3$","choice2":"$\\dfrac{1}{2}$","choice3":"$0$","choice4":"$6$","choice5":"$2$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>For any constant $a$ and any random variable $X,$ we have</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\textrm E[aX] = a \\textrm E[X].\n\\]</p>\n<p>Therefore,</p>\n<p>\\[\\begin{align*}\n\\textrm E\\left[\\dfrac{1}{2}X\\right] &= \\dfrac{1}{2} \\textrm E[X] \\\\[3pt]\n&= \\dfrac{1}{2}(6) \\\\[3pt]\n&= 3.\n\\end{align*}\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2836,"name":"Properties of Expectation for Discrete Random Variables"},"example":{"id":7418,"title":"Computing the Expected Value of a Scaled Random Variable"},"group":{"id":93945,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14263367,"answer":{"id":62369768,"cread":"2026-10-16T11:32:04.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12438},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62369792,"created":"2026-10-16T11:32:20.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":2,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12781,"number":7,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 11:32 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":109224,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7418,"text":"<p>A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.</p>\n<table rules=all cellpadding=10 align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 2mm; margin-top: 2mm\">\n\n<tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"text-align:center\">$x$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$1$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$2$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$3$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"text-align:center\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0.05$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0.15$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0.3$</td>\n</tr>\n\n\n\n</table>\n\n<p>Calculate $\\textrm E[4X].$</p>\n","choice1":"$11.2$","choice2":"$11.3$","choice3":"$11.45$","choice4":"$11.7$","choice5":"$11.85$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, let&#39;s find $\\textrm E[X].$ </p>\n<p>The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S$ is given by</p>\n<p>\\[\n\t\\textrm E[X] = \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S} x \\cdot f(x).\n\\]</p>\n<p>Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\t\\textrm E[X]\n\t\t&= \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S} x \\cdot f(x)\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&=0\\cdot 0.05+1\\cdot0.1+2\\cdot 0.15+3\\cdot 0.4+4\\cdot 0.3\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&=2.8.\n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Hence, we have </p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\t\\textrm E[4X]\n\t\t&=4\\textrm E[X]\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&=4\\cdot 2.8\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&=11.2.\n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":2836,"name":"Properties of Expectation for Discrete Random Variables"},"example":{"id":7418,"title":"Computing the Expected Value of a Scaled Random Variable"},"group":{"id":93946,"calculator":"Standard"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14263367,"answer":{"id":62369792,"cread":"2026-10-16T11:32:20.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":2,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12781},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62369887,"created":"2026-10-16T11:32:37.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12874,"number":8,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 11:32 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":84102,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":7418,"text":"<p>Compute $\\textrm E[-5X]$ if $\\textrm E[X]=-1.$</p>\n","choice1":"$5$","choice2":"$-1$","choice3":"$1$","choice4":"$-5$","choice5":"$0$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>For any constant $a$ and any random variable $X,$ we have</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\textrm E[aX] = a \\textrm E[X].\n\\]</p>\n<p>Therefore,</p>\n<p>\\[\\begin{align*}\n\\textrm E[-5X] &= -5 \\textrm E[X] \\\\[3pt]\n&= (-5)(-1) \\\\[3pt]\n&= 5.\n\\end{align*}\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2836,"name":"Properties of Expectation for Discrete Random Variables"},"example":{"id":7418,"title":"Computing the Expected Value of a Scaled Random Variable"},"group":{"id":93945,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14263367,"answer":{"id":62369887,"cread":"2026-10-16T11:32:37.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12874},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62369916,"created":"2026-10-16T11:32:55.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":3,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13978,"number":9,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 11:32 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":109225,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7418,"text":"<p>A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.</p>\n<table rules=all cellpadding=10 align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 2mm; margin-top: 2mm\">\n\n<tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"text-align:center\">$x$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$1$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$2$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$3$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"text-align:center\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0.15$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0.25$</td>\n</tr>\n\n\n\n</table>\n\n<p>Calculate $\\textrm E[-5X].$</p>\n","choice1":"$-10.75$","choice2":"$-9.75$","choice3":"$10.55$","choice4":"$-10.25$","choice5":"$11.25$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, let&#39;s find $\\textrm E[X].$ </p>\n<p>The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S$ is given by</p>\n<p>\\[\n\t\\textrm E[X] = \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S} x \\cdot f(x).\n\\]</p>\n<p>Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\t\\textrm E[X]\n\t\t&= \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S} x \\cdot f(x)\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&= 0\\cdot 0.1+1\\cdot0.3+2\\cdot 0.2+3\\cdot 0.15+4\\cdot 0.25\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&= 2.15.\n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Hence, we have </p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\t\\textrm E[-5X]\n\t\t&= -5\\textrm E[X]\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&= -5\\cdot 2.15\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&= -10.75.\n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":2836,"name":"Properties of Expectation for Discrete Random Variables"},"example":{"id":7418,"title":"Computing the Expected Value of a Scaled Random Variable"},"group":{"id":93946,"calculator":"Standard"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14263367,"answer":{"id":62369916,"cread":"2026-10-16T11:32:55.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":3,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13978},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62369948,"created":"2026-10-16T11:33:13.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12257,"number":10,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 11:33 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":109227,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7418,"text":"<p>A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.</p>\n<table rules=all cellpadding=10 align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 2mm; margin-top: 2mm\">\n\n<tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"text-align:center\">$x$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$2$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$4$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$6$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$8$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"text-align:center\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0.2$</td>\n</tr>\n\n\n\n</table>\n\n<p>Calculate $\\textrm E[-0.25X].$</p>\n","choice1":"$-1$","choice2":"$1$","choice3":"$-2$","choice4":"$0.5$","choice5":"$-0.5$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, let&#39;s find $\\textrm E[X].$ </p>\n<p>The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S$ is given by</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\textrm E[X] = \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S} x \\cdot f(x).\n\\]</p>\n<p>Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\t\\textrm E[X]\n\t\t&= \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S} x \\cdot f(x)\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&= 0\\cdot 0.3+2\\cdot 0.1+4\\cdot 0.1+6\\cdot 0.3+8\\cdot 0.2\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&= 4.\n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Hence, we have </p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\t\\textrm E[-0.25X]\n\t\t&=-0.25\\textrm E[X]\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&=-0.25\\cdot 4\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&=-1.\n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":2836,"name":"Properties of Expectation for Discrete Random Variables"},"example":{"id":7418,"title":"Computing the Expected Value of a Scaled Random Variable"},"group":{"id":93946,"calculator":"Standard"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14263367,"answer":{"id":62369948,"cread":"2026-10-16T11:33:13.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12257},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":9130,"number":3,"title":"Computing the Expected Value of a Transformed Random Variable","answers":[{"id":62369991,"created":"2026-10-16T11:33:46.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":18317,"number":11,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 11:33 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:18","question":{"id":109228,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":9130,"text":"<p>Compute $\\textrm E[-3X-2]$ if $\\textrm E[X]=-2.$</p>\n","choice1":"$4$","choice2":"$-8$","choice3":"$-4$","choice4":"$6$","choice5":"$-6$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>For any constants $a$ and $b$ and any random variable $X,$ we have</p>\n<p>\\[\n\t\\textrm E[aX+b] = a \\textrm E[X] + b.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Therefore,</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\t\\textrm E[-3X-2] \n\t\t&= -3 \\textrm E[X] - 2\\\\[3pt]\n\t\t&= -3(-2) - 2 \\\\[3pt]\n\t\t&= 4.\n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":2836,"name":"Properties of Expectation for Discrete Random Variables"},"example":{"id":9130,"title":"Computing the Expected Value of a Transformed Random Variable"},"group":{"id":93947,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14263367,"answer":{"id":62369991,"cread":"2026-10-16T11:33:46.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":18317},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62370032,"created":"2026-10-16T11:34:14.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":19264,"number":12,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 11:34 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:19","question":{"id":109299,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":9130,"text":"<p>A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.</p>\n<table rules=all cellpadding=10 align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 2mm; margin-top: 2mm\">\n\n<tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"text-align:center\">$x$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$1$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$2$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$3$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"text-align:center\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$\\dfrac{1}{6}$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$\\dfrac{1}{12}$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$\\dfrac{5}{12}$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$\\dfrac{1}{4}$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$\\dfrac{1}{12}$</td>\n</tr>\n\n\n\n</table>\n\n<p>Calculate $\\textrm E\\left[4X-8\\right].$</p>\n","choice1":"$0$","choice2":"$6$","choice3":"$\\dfrac{7}{12}$","choice4":"$\\dfrac{5}{4}$","choice5":"$\\dfrac{10}{3}$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, let&#39;s find $\\textrm E[X].$ </p>\n<p>The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S$ is given by</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\textrm E[X] = \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S} x \\cdot f(x).\n\\]</p>\n<p>Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\t\\textrm E[X]\n\t\t&= \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S} x \\cdot f(x)\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&= 0\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{6}+1\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{12}+2\\cdot \\dfrac{5}{12}+3\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{4}+4\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{12}\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&= 2.\n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Hence, we have </p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\t\\textrm E[4X-8]\n%\t\t&= \\textrm E[4X]-\\textrm E[8]\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&= 4\\textrm E[X]-8\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&= 4\\cdot 2-8\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&= 0.\n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":2836,"name":"Properties of Expectation for Discrete Random Variables"},"example":{"id":9130,"title":"Computing the Expected Value of a Transformed Random Variable"},"group":{"id":93948,"calculator":"Standard"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14263367,"answer":{"id":62370032,"cread":"2026-10-16T11:34:14.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":19264},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62370085,"created":"2026-10-16T11:34:44.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":21923,"number":13,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 11:34 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:22","question":{"id":108537,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":9130,"text":"<p>A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.</p>\n<table rules=all cellpadding=10 align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 2mm; margin-top: 2mm\">\n\n<tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"text-align:center\">$x$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$1$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$2$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$3$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"text-align:center\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0.15$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0.3$</td>\n</tr>\n\n\n\n</table>\n\n<p>Calculate $\\textrm E[5X+4].$</p>\n","choice1":"$15.75$","choice2":"$13.75$","choice3":"$17.45$","choice4":"$16.85$","choice5":"$18.15$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, let&#39;s find $\\textrm E[X].$ </p>\n<p>The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S$ is given by</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\textrm E[X] = \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S} x \\cdot f(x).\n\\]</p>\n<p>Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\\textrm E[X]\n&= \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S} x \\cdot f(x)\\\\[5pt]\n&=0\\cdot 0.1+1\\cdot0.2+2\\cdot 0.25+3\\cdot 0.15+4\\cdot 0.3\\\\[5pt]\n&=2.35.\n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Hence, we have </p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\\textrm E[5X+4]\n&=\\textrm E[5X]+\\textrm E[4]\\\\[5pt]\n&=5\\textrm E[X]+4\\\\[5pt]\n&=5\\cdot 2.35+4\\\\[5pt]\n&=15.75.\n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":2836,"name":"Properties of Expectation for Discrete Random Variables"},"example":{"id":9130,"title":"Computing the Expected Value of a Transformed Random Variable"},"group":{"id":93948,"calculator":"Standard"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14263367,"answer":{"id":62370085,"cread":"2026-10-16T11:34:44.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":21923},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62370137,"created":"2026-10-16T11:35:15.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":25443,"number":14,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 11:35 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:25","question":{"id":109298,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":9130,"text":"<p>A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.</p>\n<table rules=all cellpadding=10 align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 2mm; margin-top: 2mm\">\n\n<tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"text-align:center\">$x$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$0$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$5$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$10$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$15$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$20$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"text-align:center\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$\\dfrac{1}{4}$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$\\dfrac{1}{8}$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$\\dfrac{1}{4}$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$\\dfrac{1}{8}$</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">$\\dfrac{1}{4}$</td>\n</tr>\n\n\n\n</table>\n\n<p>Calculate $\\textrm E\\left[-\\dfrac{3}{2}X-5\\right].$</p>\n","choice1":"$-20$","choice2":"$15$","choice3":"$10$","choice4":"$20$","choice5":"$-10$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, let&#39;s find $\\textrm E[X].$ </p>\n<p>The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S$ is given by</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\textrm E[X] = \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S} x \\cdot f(x).\n\\]</p>\n<p>Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\t\\textrm E[X]\n\t\t&= \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S} x \\cdot f(x)\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&= 0\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{4} +5\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{8}+10\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{4}+15\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{8}+20\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{4}\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&= 10.\n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Hence, we have </p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\t\\textrm E\\left[-\\dfrac{3}{2}X-5 \\right]\n\t\t&= -\\dfrac{3}{2}\\textrm E[X] - 5\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&= -\\dfrac{3}{2}\\cdot 10 - 5\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&= -20.\n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":2836,"name":"Properties of Expectation for Discrete Random Variables"},"example":{"id":9130,"title":"Computing the Expected Value of a Transformed Random Variable"},"group":{"id":93948,"calculator":"Standard"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14263367,"answer":{"id":62370137,"cread":"2026-10-16T11:35:15.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":25443},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62370167,"created":"2026-10-16T11:35:33.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12589,"number":15,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 11:35 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":109232,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":9130,"text":"<p>Compute $\\textrm E[5X-7]$ if $\\textrm E[X]=-2.$</p>\n","choice1":"$-17$","choice2":"$-10$","choice3":"$14$","choice4":"$-35$","choice5":"$17$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>For any constants $a$ and $b$ and any random variable $X,$ we have</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\textrm E[aX+b] = a \\textrm E[X] + b.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Therefore,</p>\n<p>\\[\\begin{align*}\n\\textrm E[5X-7] &= 5 \\textrm E[X] -7\\\\[3pt]\n&= 5(-2) -7 \\\\[3pt]\n&= -17.\n\\end{align*}\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2836,"name":"Properties of Expectation for Discrete Random Variables"},"example":{"id":9130,"title":"Computing the Expected Value of a Transformed Random Variable"},"group":{"id":93947,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14263367,"answer":{"id":62370167,"cread":"2026-10-16T11:35:33.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12589},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]}],"localGraph":{"topicId":2836,"topics":[{"id":730,"name":"Expected Values of Discrete Random Variables","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"halfLife":0.46637793984802045,"repetition":1,"stability":0.11559778032820772},{"id":2836,"name":"Properties of Expectation for Discrete Random Variables","prerequisites":[730,3631],"frontier":0,"halfLife":1.2580740615761754,"repetition":2,"stability":0.17582213660478127},{"id":3292,"name":"Expected Values of Sums and Products of Random Variables","prerequisites":[2836],"frontier":1,"halfLife":0.1,"repetition":0,"stability":0},{"id":3631,"name":"One-to-One Transformations of Discrete Random Variables","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"halfLife":13.416570919231985,"repetition":3,"stability":0.4281191963662141},{"id":3642,"name":"Moments of Discrete Random Variables","prerequisites":[2836],"frontier":0,"halfLife":0.1,"repetition":0,"stability":0},{"id":4012,"name":"Expected Values of Continuous Random Variables","prerequisites":[2836],"frontier":0,"halfLife":0.1,"repetition":0,"stability":0}]}}}